    <h2>Apply for our fellowship</h2>
    <p>How can we use the world's resources to best help others? How can we tackle some of the world's most pressing problems, including ending global poverty and factory farming, mitigating technological risks, preventing future pandemics, and stopping climate change? How can WashU students find fulfilling and impactful careers?</p>
    <p>The fellowship is a five-week long program that engages with these questions and explores the core concepts and ideas within the effective altruism community. We hope the fellowship will provide you with a framework for figuring out how you can make a difference in the world.</p>
    <p>We highly recommend applying to this program if you:</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Want to get to know other WashU students</li>
      <li>Are interested in learning about philosophy, economics, philanthropy, rationality, and/or moral progress</li>
      <li>Want to make a large positive impact through your career or donations, but aren't sure how to do that</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Applications for the spring 2027 fellowship will open in January.</p>
